# Decided
Purposes, old -> new:
- traversal/node_tuple.h: "flatten an expression tree into the types of
  its nodes." -> "... of its leaves." Only the primary template yields
  std::tuple<T>; every specialization yields its children (where,
  operators, select, function calls) or nothing (aliases, into, the
  implicit join constraint) - the order get_prepared_statement.h lines
  up with the leaves ast_iterator hands to its callable.
- serialization/streaming.h: "stream the pieces of SQL text that many
  statements share." -> "stream pieces of SQL text into the statement
  being written." Several modes have one caller (compound expressions,
  column constraints of a schema definition, a CTE's constraints), and
  the sharing is a relation: the Intention names it ("used by the
  statement serializer and by execution/ ..."). trueqbit asked whether
  the Purpose needs "shared" or the Intention holds it; Claude: the
  Intention, the Purpose keeps the reason.
- serialization/quoting.h: "quote identifiers and literal values for
  SQL text." -> "quote identifiers and string literals for SQL text."
  lang_expr.html#literal_values_constants_: literal values are
  "integers, floating point numbers, strings, BLOBs, or NULLs"; "BLOB
  literals are string literals containing hexadecimal data".
- order_by_serializer.h: fixed by the refactor d43e0e69, its Purpose
  unchanged.
Held, Claude's leans:
- column_expressions_collector.h (reviewer: wider than a select's
  result columns, uncertain): the columns/struct serializer
  (statement_serializer.h, the use_parentheses branch) runs alone only
  in tests/statement_serializer_tests/select_constraints.cpp:20; a
  select's own columns go through collect_column_expressions(sel.col).
- "expression tree" in ast_iterator.h, node_tuple.h,
  table_name_collector.h: the tree's term (source-layout.md "Walking an
  expression tree"; a prepared statement's node is its `expression`),
  though SQLite's `expr` is narrower.
- statement_serializer's name, narrower than its Purpose: taken as
  given; ledger.
- serializer_context.h, a Purpose restating the name: trueqbit's ruling
  of this round; campaign.md "When the header adds to the name".
- Clean per the reviewer: default_value_serialization.h,
  cte_column_names.h, table_name_collector.h, statement_serializer.h,
  ast_iterator.h.
- serialization-round/serialization_headers.py carries the new
  Purposes, so a rerun on a clean tree writes them.

